<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2817" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Anthĕmūs</span></b> ,
		untis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀνθεμοῦς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A region in Macedonia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 10,
				17, § 36</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town in Mesopotamia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 26,
				30, § 118</span></i>; called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Anthĕmūsĭăs</span></b> ,
				ădis (sc. urbs), <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 6,
			41</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A river of Colchis</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 5,
				5, § 15</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Anthĕ-mūsĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>pertaining to Anthemus</i>, <i><span class="en">Eutr. 8,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
